{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolvsgroup", "label": "Pool vs group", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two ways a router acquires routees, encoding very different lifecycle relationships. The local Router is always a pool; ClusterRouter is always a group."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolrouter", "label": "Pool router", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## Pool router", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The router owns its routees as children, so lifecycle is coupled (stop the router and all routees stop, no orphans), supervision is straightforward and a crashed routee is restarted. The costs: routees are stateless from the router's perspective, size is fixed at spawn time, and their names are auto-generated routee-1..N. Right shape for homogeneous worker pools."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_grouprouter", "label": "Group router (cluster only)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## Group router *(cluster only)*", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The router finds routees rather than creating them, so lifecycle is independent and sizing follows topology - add a node and it is picked up with no restart. The costs: you must spawn the routees on every node, an empty pool drops messages into dead letters with a warning, and supervision is per-node with the router having no authority. Right shape for fixed-name workers across a cluster."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_threequestions", "label": "Three questions to decide between them", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## Three concrete questions to decide between them", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Do the routees hold per-instance state that matters, does the pool size need to change at runtime, and should stopping the router cascade-stop the routees. If two of three point one way that is the model; if they conflict, the mismatch is telling you something about how the routees should relate to the router."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_clusterpoolnotexposed", "label": "Cluster-aware pool routers are not exposed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## A common confusion: cluster-aware *pool* routers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Other toolkits have a cluster-pool that spawns its own routees across nodes; actor-ts does not - the cluster router is always group-shaped. The equivalent is a per-node deployment actor spawning local routees plus a ClusterRouter targeting them by path."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_stoppingbehaviorcompared", "label": "Stopping behavior compared", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## Stopping behavior, compared", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The asymmetry matters for graceful shutdown: a pool router folds cleanly when the system terminates, while a group router leaves behind routees on other nodes that do not know this caller is gone."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolvsgroup", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolrouter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolvsgroup", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_grouprouter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolvsgroup", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_threequestions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolvsgroup", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_clusterpoolnotexposed", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolvsgroup", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_stoppingbehaviorcompared", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolrouter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## Pool router", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolrouter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_scatter_gather_scattergather", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_grouprouter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_clusterrouterform", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## Group router *(cluster only)*", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolrouter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## Pool router", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolvsgroup", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_strategies_routingstrategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/pool-vs-group.mdx", "source_location": "## Where to next", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}